  "description": "Jackson §12.3 (motion in combined, uniform, static electric and magnetic fields). In crossed fields a particle starting at rest does not follow E: it rolls along a cycloid and drifts with the velocity E×B/B², whatever its charge and mass. A positive and a negative ion start here; both drift to the right, rolling in opposite senses. Their guiding centres follow the equipotentials (see the potential map): place a charge to bend the drift of both into the detector.",
